                <pb facs="0454" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1933v02/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.4016/362: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy (Garrett) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1933-04-03T19:00:00+01:00">April 3, 1933—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 3—2:20 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. The British Ambassador tells me that in a talk this afternoon with the Chief
                    of the Government, Mussolini told him that he was continuing to make the
                    strongest possible representations at Berlin against the anti-Jewish action of
                    the Hitler Government and that he, Mussolini, believed this agitation would
                    shortly cease.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Garrett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
